    "behaviors": [
      {
        "id": "B001",
        "text": "After page handlers are marked with `@expose`, calling a WSGI `Application` rooted at that object with a matching `PATH_INFO` and `HTTP_HOST` returns HTTP 200 and the handler body."
      },
      {
        "id": "B002",
        "text": "A request whose `PATH_INFO` matches no exposed handler is answered with an HTTP 404 status."
      },
      {
        "id": "B003",
        "text": "Decorating a function with `Tool('before_handler', hook, name='flag')()` sets `function._cp_config['tools.flag.on']` to True."
      },
      {
        "id": "B004",
        "text": "An exposed nested object attribute is dispatched when `PATH_INFO` names that nested path, returning the nested handler body with HTTP 200."
      },
      {
        "id": "B005",
        "text": "The package exposes `Application`, `Dispatcher`, `expose`, and `Tool` with the callable signatures listed in this contract."
